  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a clean, minimal baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: one modality, one profile, a standard linear encoder, and no aggregation or fusion. This gives a well-defined reference accuracy for the RNA modality. In subsequent experiments I can then test image-only (config_010), compare RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), and evaluate whether multimodal fusion adds value over the best single modality. Starting with the simplest baseline avoids confounding multiple design choices and provides the most interpretable anchor point for the 9 remaining experiments."
